Base64 — standalone Rust Tezbar extension

Rust port of the MIT-licensed Raycast `base64` extension
(https://github.com/raycast/extensions, path extensions/base64, upstream commit
6734d85992290066fd31a7f5bee3cca3d3545a1a). Original author DanielSinclair;
contributors stelo, sammarks, ridemountainpig, luisafk. Tezbar adaptation by
almatkai. See LICENSE and licenses/raycast-extensions-MIT.txt.

resources/assets/command-icon.png is the unchanged original Raycast PNG
(80527 bytes, SHA-256 91b4ccba2a5abfaf8eb4541073a5bc10e06b8349a94b0c33538ebf8f0a2eca8c).
No trademark rights are claimed.
The executable also links the Tezbar Rust extension SDK (Apache-2.0).
Its original LICENSE and NOTICE, and the resolved dependency notices for both
published targets, are preserved under licenses/crates/; see licenses/THIRD_PARTY.md.
